.Dd October 13, 2026
.Dt GIT-GUD 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm git-gud
.Nd manage git-gud repository hooks
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm install
.Op Fl f | Fl -force
.Op Ar directory
.Nm
.Cm version
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
installs and runs git lua hooks for repository automation.
.Pp
The installed hooks load a Lua configuration file and run registered handlers for
Git events.
By default the configuration is read from
.Pa ~/.config/git/gud.lua
when it exists, otherwise
.Pa ~/.config/git-gud/init.lua .
Set
.Ev GIT_GUD_INIT
to use a different configuration file.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width install
.It Cm install Op Fl f | Fl -force Op Ar directory
Install
.Nm
into the specified hooks directory and link supported hook names to it.
If no directory is specified, use the current repository's hooks directory.
The specified directory must already exist; it does not need to belong to a Git repository.
Refuses to overwrite an existing installation unless
.Fl f
or
.Fl -force
is supplied.
.It Cm version
Print the command version and, when installed in the current repository, the hook
version.
.El
.Sh HOOKS
The supported hooks are:
.Bl -tag -width post-checkout
.It Cm post-checkout
Runs after a checkout and invokes registered Lua checkout handlers.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width GIT_GUD_TRACE_FILE
.It Ev GIT_GUD_INIT
Path to the Lua configuration file. Defaults to
.Pa ~/.config/git/gud.lua
when it exists, otherwise
.Pa ~/.config/git-gud/init.lua .
.It Ev GIT_GUD_TRACE_FILE
Enable tracing. If set to an empty value, trace output is written to standard
error; otherwise trace output is written to the named file.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr git 1 ,
.Xr githooks 5
